MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE not enabled with torch.distributed.init_process_group
I had the following code in c++ to use torch.distributed-intialized MPI processes. However I got supportProvided != MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE when running these c++ code after import torch.distributed as dist;dist.init_process_group(backend='mpi')
  int supportProvided;
  int initialized;
  int initSuccess;
  MPI_Initialized(&initialized);
  if (!initialized){
    initSuccess = MPI_Init_thread(NULL, NULL, MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE, &supportProvided);
  }
  else {
    MPI_Query_thread(&supportProvided);
    initSuccess = MPI_SUCCESS;
  }
  if (initSuccess != MPI_SUCCESS) {
    MPI_Abort(MPI_COMM_WORLD, initSuccess);
  }

  if (supportProvided != MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE) {
        std::cout<<"MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE not supported by installed MPI library")<<std::endl;
